# Independent actual-six review

PASS for the bounded revocation-confirmation increment. A separate read-only source/log audit verified six passing real-PostgreSQL cases, exit0, with no setup or collection failure. Source hashes match all eleven frozen pins, including Slack 2fece3be, service 9b8374ac and native definitions 790c3800. No test was rerun for the audit.

The invalid_auth, revoked:false and missing-confirmation cases preserve exact encrypted credentials and account/settings/scopes/history facts, retain pending status, emit zero disconnected events and block ordinary token access. Explicit revoked:true and token_revoked clear credentials and record exactly one correctly attributed disconnected event. The manual ambiguous-to-confirmed retry preserves pending bytes first and then completes one transition without another OAuth exchange.

The actual command took3.294215seconds; command through cleanup14.070198seconds; whole invocation14.323396seconds. Terminal evidence records no owned processes/new containers, three foreign containers with unchanged state, unchanged network/volume sets, unchanged source and no forced removal. Bun1.4.4/hash, no-env flags and automatic dotenv absences match. Normal pressure1, available memory50 to51percent.

The result accumulator reports a sampled host-group maximum352720KiB. Only two observation rows are retained, whose maximum is260368KiB. The frozen recipe samples/update its maximum every0.2seconds but persists an observation row only every2seconds; this explains the different sampling resolution. The individual intermediate maximum is not retained and cannot be reconstructed from the coarse rows. No continuous or Docker-inclusive aggregate peak is claimed.

The six cases do not establish in-flight race ordering, concurrent reconnect/revocation, durable worker retries, browser/native-auth or real-provider behavior. token_expired/account_inactive are unit-covered, not additional native paths. These remain separate scope, without adding gates to this bounded increment or claiming whole CONN-017/018 acceptance.

Main still owns current-source reconciliation, configured type/lint checks, reviewed privacy metadata, regenerated canonical inventory, exact-source CI and publication. No canonical task count, release, deployment or installation status changes follow from this audit.
